course: dictionary
lesson: 3511
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. The word father is a good example.
explain: «A baby starts when a tiny cell from the mother and a tiny cell from the father join together.» Here father means a man who has a child, a dad. The words mother, baby and cell tell you it is about a parent.
explain: A father can also be a man who looks after a child as a parent, like a stepfather. Father can be a title too, for some priests. Another meaning is the person who started something. Read the words around it to see which one fits.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Father is a noun, and it can also be a verb. As a verb, to father means to become the father of a child.
fact: «The fathers eat nothing for about two months» is about male emperor penguins keeping their eggs warm in the cold.
fact: A father can be a dad, a stepfather, or a man who cares for a child as a parent.
fact: Father is also a title for some priests, so it does not always mean a dad.
fact: The father of something is the person who started it, so the same word can describe a family or an idea.
exercise: «A baby starts when a tiny cell from the mother and a tiny cell from the father join together.» What does father mean here? | *A man who has a child, a dad | A title for a priest | The person who started a club | A bird that sits on eggs
exercise: The club was set up by Sam, so people call him the father of the club. What does father mean here? | A man who has a child in the club | *The person who started it | A dad to all the members | A priest who leads the club
exercise: «The father sits on the eggs for about 8 weeks, hardly eating.» Which animal is the father in this sentence? | A horse | A penguin | A baby bird | *An emu
test: «Father Murphy led the service at the church.» What does Father mean here? | A stepfather | A dad | The person who started the church | *A priest
test: What does it mean to father a child? | To feed a child | To teach a class | To walk a dog | *To become the father of a child
exam: Which sentence uses father to mean the person who started something? | The emperor penguin father keeps the egg warm | *The father of the idea was the first to write it down | My father drives me to school | Father Brown led the prayers today
